%% alt: An eval loop. Cases from real use, edge cases and must-refuse cases run through the system under test (prompt, model, retrieval and tools). Graders, which may be code, a model or people, score the outputs and transcripts, giving scores with error bars that feed a release gate. Production traffic is sampled into the graders, and people read outputs regularly to refine the criteria and add cases.
flowchart TB
  D[(Eval cases: real use,<br/>edge cases, must-refuse)]:::data --> S[System under test<br/>prompt, model, retrieval, tools]:::model
  S --> O[Outputs and transcripts]:::data --> G[Graders<br/>code, model, human]:::control
  G --> R[Scores with error bars]:::data --> X{Release gate}:::control
  P[Production traffic]:::human -.->|sample| G
  O -.->|read regularly| H[People refine<br/>criteria and cases]:::human -.-> D
